{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c673","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a834-2dd6-7302-a20b-bd6ef471e4be"},"sequence":404,"recorded_at":1780531400000803,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f40cada4-f145-4b44-bc35-1e9f8e45782b","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f40cada4-f145-4b44-bc35-1e9f8e45782b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f40cada4-f145-4b44-bc35-1e9f8e45782b"},"call_id":"call_01a0a83557567490a4084824f4bbb21f","text":"Read text file `RELEASING.md`.\n1|# Release operations\n2|\n3|## One-time setup on macbook-iv\n4|\n5|The release workflow uses this Mac's manually controlled runner. Enable it in Runner Control before releasing; a disabled runner leaves the workflow queued. Pull requests run unit tests on GitHub-hosted macOS and do not use release credentials.\n6|\n7|Required tools: Xcode, Tuist 4.9.0, GitHub CLI, Python 3. The workflow installs Go 1.25.5 and builds the scaffold generator at a pinned revision. Sparkle tools are downloaded at a pinned version and verified by SHA-256.\n8|\n9|The runner's login Keychain needs:\n10|\n11|- A Developer ID Application certificate **and matching private key** for team `262RZ595FP`. Apple Development and certificates belonging to other teams are rejected.\n12|- A validated notarytool profile named `RunnerControl-notary`.\n13|- The existing Sparkle Ed25519 signing key under account `works.relux.runnercontrol`. Keep a secure backup; losing it prevents updates to installed releases. Do not regenerate it for each release.\n14|\n15|An Apple Account Holder must issue the Developer ID certificate from the supplied CSR. Import the issued certificate together with its matching private key. Use `xcrun notarytool store-credentials` locally with a valid App Store Connect API key, key ID and issuer ID; it validates authorization before saving the profile. Never commit keys, certificates with private keys, or credentials.\n16|\n17|Run `./Scripts/release-preflight.sh` from any directory to verify these prerequisites. Keychain access must work from the runner session without an unattended authorization prompt.\n18|\n19|## Publish\n20|\n21|1. Set `marketing_version` in `ios-app-manager.json` to the intended version and regenerate with the pinned macOS app generator.\n22|2. Commit to `main` and wait for the Tests workflow.\n23|3. Tag that commit `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` and push the tag. Alternatively run **Release DMG** with that existing tag.\n24|4. The workflow tests, archives, exports with Developer ID, notarizes/staples the app and DMG, generates the Sparkle signature, and checks feed metadata.\n25|5. Only after those checks does it create a draft release, upload `RunnerControl.dmg`, `appcast.xml` and `SHA256SUMS`, then publish it as latest. Assets remain in GitHub Releases without the artifact retention deadline.\n26|\n27|Each feed points to its immutable version-specific DMG URL. The application follows the latest release's appcast. Published release assets are never overwritten by the workflow. If uploading fails after draft creation, inspect the draft and remove the incomplete draft before retrying the same run. Diagnostic logs are retained for 14 days.\n28|\n29|Build numbers are derived from the release workflow run number and attempt. Keep this workflow's run counter continuous; do not replace it with a new workflow whose counter starts over without adjusting the build-number scheme.\n30|\n31|## Exact requirements reference\n32|\n33|Every value below is enforced by the named script and covered by `Scripts/tests`. If a value changes, update the script, this section, and the tests together.\n34|\n35|| Requirement | Exact value | Enforced by |\n36||---|---|---|\n37|| Signing identity | Exactly one `Developer ID Application` certificate with private key for team `262RZ595FP`; Apple Development and other teams are refused | `release-preflight.sh`, `release_metadata.py signing-identity`, `release.sh` DMG signing |\n38|| Bundle and team | `works.relux.runnercontrol` / `262RZ595FP` | `release_metadata.py prepare` |\n39|| Release tag | `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, equal to `marketing_version`, on `main` ancestry at `HEAD`; an existing release refuses the run | `release.yml` tag validation, `prepare` |\n40|| Build number | `project_version` = `(100 + run).attempt` with run 1..9899 and attempt 1..99 (for example run 1 attempt 1 → `101.1`) | `release_metadata.py prepare` |\n41|| Notary profile | `RunnerControl-notary` in the runner's login keychain, unlocked in the runner session; `notarytool` waits up to 30 minutes per artifact (app ZIP, then DMG) and only `Accepted` proceeds | `release-preflight.sh`, `release.sh` notarize |\n42|| Sparkle account and feed | Account `works.relux.runnercontrol`; private key must match `SUPublicEDKey`; feed `https://github.com/relux-works/runner-control/releases/latest/download/appcast.xml` | `release-preflight.sh`, `prepare` |\n43|| Sparkle tools | Version `2.10.0`, SHA-256 `c2bf58aa8387266ac179357b1415d6f2635f044da8be41042af32425dae6da0c` | `sparkle-tools.sh` |\n44|| Appcast | Exactly one item; `sparkle:version` = build, `shortVersionString` = marketing version, enclosure URL `https://github.com/relux-works/runner-control/releases/download/<tag>/RunnerControl.dmg`, 64-byte `edSignature`, `length` = DMG bytes, minimum macOS 14 | `release_metadata.py verify` |\n45|| Scaffold generator | `skill-ios-app-manager` at `755a29538dfe0867671ac4291b016bf42d93a299`, built with Go `1.25.5` | `release.yml` |\n46|| Host tools | Xcode, Tuist 4.9.0, GitHub CLI, Python 3, plus `xcodebuild xcrun codesign security hdiutil tuist gh python3` on `PATH` | `release-preflight.sh` |\n47|| Publish order | Preflight → unit tests → package/notarize/verify → draft → upload DMG + appcast + SHA256SUMS → publish as latest; the publish step runs only after a successful package and never overwrites published assets | `release.yml`, `release.sh` |\n48|\n49|## Failure recovery\n50|\n51|Release run 35040921163 (`v1.1.0`) failed in Release prerequisites before any\n52|build or signing: the login keychain was locked in the runner session, so\n53|`notarytool` could not read profile `RunnerControl-notary` (`keychainLocked`).\n54|No draft or published release was created.\n55|\n56|Per coordinator directive, `v1.1.0` is neither retried nor deleted: the tag\n57|stays as-is with no release, and the approved next release is new `v1.2.0`\n58|after product integration. No new tag is created and nothing is published\n59|until product review and coordinator dispatch.\n60|\n61|If a future run reports a locked keychain in Release prerequisites, unlock\n62|the login keychain on macbook-iv with a console login as the runner user (no\n63|credentials are printed or exported), enable the runner in Runner Control,\n64|then run **Release DMG** via workflow_dispatch with the existing tag. Do not\n65|delete or re-push the tag and do not create the release by hand; the workflow\n66|refuses to overwrite published assets. If prerequisites still report a locked\n67|keychain, the runner session has no unlocked login keychain; unlock it and\n68|dispatch again.\n69|\n70|Preflight also fails fast when no Developer ID Application identity for team\n71|`262RZ595FP` is present, when several are present (remove the stale\n72|certificate so signing is unambiguous), when the notarytool profile is missing\n73|(recreate it with `xcrun notarytool store-credentials` as above), when the\n74|Sparkle private key does not match `SUPublicEDKey`, or when signing\n75|identities cannot be read at all (a failed read is reported as unknown,\n76|never as missing or verified).\n77|\n78|Apple notarization waits up to 30 minutes per artifact (app ZIP, then DMG). If\n79|a wait times out, the submission ID in the release logs can be inspected with\n80|`xcrun notarytool info <id> --keychain-profile RunnerControl-notary` (status\n81|only); retrying dispatches a new run with a new monotonic build number. A\n82|pending signing-check submission is not a release artifact and does not block\n83|the next release.\n84|\n85|## Validation status\n86|\n87|Core and release metadata tests pass locally and in GitHub Actions; the Sparkle-enabled app builds successfully. Developer ID signing and the notarytool profile are validated on macbook-iv. The complete notarization and update-install cycle requires the first accepted Apple submission and two published versions. Check GitHub Releases for publication status.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c675","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a834-2dd6-7302-a20b-bd6ef471e4be"},"sequence":405,"recorded_at":1780531400000805,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f40cada4-f145-4b44-bc35-1e9f8e45782b","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f40cada4-f145-4b44-bc35-1e9f8e45782b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f40cada4-f145-4b44-bc35-1e9f8e45782b"},"call_id":"call_01a0a835588477c5a203a3b28cbea24c","text":"Read text file `Scripts/tests/test_release_preflight.py`.\n1|\"\"\"Drive Scripts/release-preflight.sh with stubbed macOS tools.\n2|\n3|Each test builds an isolated repo root (preflight + sparkle-tools scripts,\n4|minimal ios-app-manager.json, stub Sparkle tools so no download happens) and\n5|a stub bin dir shadowing xcrun/security. Real python3/bash/grep run from PATH.\n6|No credentials enter the fixtures.\n7|\"\"\"\n8|import base64\n9|import json\n10|import os\n11|from pathlib import Path\n12|import shlex\n13|import shutil\n14|import subprocess\n15|import tempfile\n16|import unittest\n17|\n18|REPO = Path(__file__).parents[2]\n19|PUBKEY = base64.b64encode(bytes(32)).decode()\n20|WRONG_PUBKEY = base64.b64encode(bytes(range(32))).decode()\n21|TEAM_LINE = '  3) 267D90FC976A48CF830BE7F41AE612999E025054 \"Developer ID Application: Relux Works, LLC (262RZ595FP)\"'\n22|OTHER_LINES = ('  1) 7FB8D981868F2637B75DFD098A1F87E0CC11158D \"Apple Development: Ivan Oparin (45W9YW7M6V)\"\\n'\n23|               '  4) C8448515B5871071F90EB0168A79DCD35E7CA9FE \"Developer ID Application: SKL VC DMCC (4Y4UJAT8QR)\"')\n24|\n25|\n26|def write_exe(path, content):\n27|    path.write_text(content)\n28|    path.chmod(0o755)\n29|\n30|\n31|class PreflightHarness(unittest.TestCase):\n32|    def setUp(self):\n33|        self.tmp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n34|        root = Path(self.tmp.name)\n35|        scripts = root / 'Scripts'\n36|        scripts.mkdir()\n37|        for name in ('release-preflight.sh', 'sparkle-tools.sh'):\n38|            shutil.copy(REPO / 'Scripts' / name, scripts / name)\n39|        (root / 'ios-app-manager.json').write_text(json.dumps(\n40|            {'macos': {'info_plist': {'SUPublicEDKey': PUBKEY}}}))\n41|        sparkle_bin = root / '.temp' / 'tools' / 'Sparkle-2.10.0' / 'bin'\n42|        sparkle_bin.mkdir(parents=True)\n43|        write_exe(sparkle_bin / 'generate_appcast', '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n')\n44|        self.sparkle_bin = sparkle_bin\n45|        self.bindir = root / 'bin'\n46|        self.bindir.mkdir()\n47|        for tool in ('xcodebuild', 'codesign', 'hdiutil', 'tuist', 'gh'):\n48|            write_exe(self.bindir / tool, '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n')\n49|        self.root = root\n50|\n51|    def tearDown(self):\n52|        self.tmp.cleanup()\n53|\n54|    def run_preflight(self, security_out, xcrun_script, sparkle_key=PUBKEY, profile=None,\n55|                      security_exit=0, security_err=''):\n56|        stub = '#!/bin/sh\\n'\n57|        if security_err:\n58|            stub += 'echo ' + shlex.quote(security_err) + ' >&2\\n'\n59|        if security_out:\n60|            stub += 'cat <<\\'EOF\\'\\n' + security_out + '\\nEOF\\n'\n61|        stub += 'exit ' + str(security_exit) + '\\n'\n62|        write_exe(self.bindir / 'security', stub)\n63|        write_exe(self.bindir / 'xcrun', xcrun_script)\n64|        write_exe(self.sparkle_bin / 'generate_keys', '#!/bin/sh\\necho ' + sparkle_key + '\\n')\n65|        env = dict(os.environ)\n66|        env['PATH'] = str(self.bindir) + os.pathsep + env['PATH']\n67|        if profile is None:\n68|            env.pop('NOTARY_PROFILE', None)\n69|        else:\n70|            env['NOTARY_PROFILE'] = profile\n71|        return subprocess.run(['bash', str(self.root / 'Scripts' / 'release-preflight.sh')],\n72|                              capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60, env=env, cwd=self.tmp.name)\n73|\n74|\n75|class ReleasePreflightTests(PreflightHarness):\n76|    def test_preflight_passes_with_valid_credentials(self):\n77|        r = self.run_preflight(OTHER_LINES + '\\n' + TEAM_LINE, '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n')\n78|        self.assertEqual(r.returncode, 0, r.stderr)\n79|        self.assertIn('Release prerequisites verified', r.stdout)\n80|        self.assertIn('RunnerControl-notary', r.stdout)\n81|\n82|    def test_locked_keychain_fails_with_unlock_guidance(self):\n83|        stub = ('#!/bin/sh\\necho \\'Error: keychainLocked(keychainName: \"default\", keychainURL: nil)'\n84|                ' Use Keychain Access or the `security unlock-keychain` command line tool'\n85|                ' to unlock the default keychain.\\' >&2\\nexit 1\\n')\n86|        r = self.run_preflight(OTHER_LINES + '\\n' + TEAM_LINE, stub)\n87|        self.assertNotEqual(r.returncode, 0)\n88|        self.assertIn('locked', r.stderr)\n89|        self.assertIn('workflow_dispatch', r.stderr)\n90|        self.assertIn('RunnerControl-notary', r.stderr)\n91|\n92|    def test_missing_profile_names_profile_without_locked_guidance(self):\n93|        stub = ('#!/bin/sh\\necho \"Error: No Keychain password item found for profile: Custom-Profile-9\" >&2\\n'\n94|                'echo \"Run \\'notarytool store-credentials\\' to create another credential profile.\" >&2\\nexit 1\\n')\n95|        r = self.run_preflight(OTHER_LINES + '\\n' + TEAM_LINE, stub, profile='Custom-Profile-9')\n96|        self.assertNotEqual(r.returncode, 0)\n97|        self.assertIn('Custom-Profile-9', r.stderr)\n98|        self.assertIn('store-credentials', r.stderr)\n99|        self.assertIn('missing from the login keychain', r.stderr)\n100|        self.assertNotIn('locked', r.stderr)\n101|\n102|    def test_missing_identity_rejected(self):\n103|        r = self.run_preflight(OTHER_LINES, '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n')\n104|        self.assertNotEqual(r.returncode, 0)\n105|        self.assertIn('Missing Developer ID Application identity', r.stderr)\n106|\n107|    def test_multiple_team_identities_rejected(self):\n108|        second = TEAM_LINE.replace('267D90FC976A48CF830BE7F41AE612999E025054',\n109|                                   'AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA').replace('  3)', '  5)')\n110|        r = self.run_preflight(OTHER_LINES + '\\n' + TEAM_LINE + '\\n' + second, '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n')\n111|        self.assertNotEqual(r.returncode, 0)\n112|        self.assertIn('Multiple Developer ID Application identities', r.stderr)\n113|\n114|    def test_sparkle_key_mismatch_rejected(self):\n115|        r = self.run_preflight(OTHER_LINES + '\\n' + TEAM_LINE, '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n', sparkle_key=WRONG_PUBKEY)\n116|        self.assertNotEqual(r.returncode, 0)\n117|        self.assertIn('Sparkle signing key', r.stderr)\n118|\n119|    def test_failed_identity_read_with_empty_output_is_unknown_not_missing(self):\n120|        r = self.run_preflight('', '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n',\n121|                               security_exit=42, security_err='security: read failed')\n122|        self.assertNotEqual(r.returncode, 0)\n123|        self.assertIn('Could not read signing identities', r.stderr)\n124|        self.assertNotIn('Missing Developer ID Application identity', r.stderr)\n125|        self.assertNotIn('Release prerequisites verified', r.stdout)\n126|\n127|    def test_failed_identity_read_with_partial_output_is_not_verified(self):\n128|        r = self.run_preflight(OTHER_LINES + '\\n' + TEAM_LINE, '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n',\n129|                               security_exit=42, security_err='security: read failed')\n130|        self.assertNotEqual(r.returncode, 0)\n131|        self.assertIn('Could not read signing identities', r.stderr)\n132|        self.assertNotIn('Release prerequisites verified', r.stdout)\n133|\n134|    def test_apple_development_same_team_rejected(self):\n135|        same_team_dev = ('  1) 7FB8D981868F2637B75DFD098A1F87E0CC11158D '\n136|                         '\"Apple Development: Ivan Oparin (262RZ595FP)\"')\n137|        other_team_devid = ('  4) C8448515B5871071F90EB0168A79DCD35E7CA9FE '\n138|                            '\"Developer ID Application: SKL VC DMCC (4Y4UJAT8QR)\"')\n139|        r = self.run_preflight(same_team_dev + '\\n' + other_team_devid, '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n')\n140|        self.assertNotEqual(r.returncode, 0)\n141|        self.assertIn('Missing Developer ID Application identity', r.stderr)\n142|        self.assertNotIn('Release prerequisites verified', r.stdout)\n143|\n144|    def test_missing_tool_rejected(self):\n145|        (self.bindir / 'tuist').unlink()\n146|        write_exe(self.bindir / 'security', '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n')\n147|        write_exe(self.bindir / 'xcrun', '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n')\n148|        env = dict(os.environ)\n149|        env['PATH'] = str(self.bindir)\n150|        bash = shutil.which('bash')\n151|        self.assertTrue(bash, 'absolute bash path required for the isolated-PATH probe')\n152|        r = subprocess.run([bash, str(self.root / 'Scripts' / 'release-preflight.sh')],\n153|                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60, env=env, cwd=self.tmp.name)\n154|        self.assertNotEqual(r.returncode, 0)\n155|        self.assertIn('Missing release tool: tuist', r.stderr)\n156|        self.assertNotIn('Release prerequisites verified', r.stdout)\n157|\n158|    def test_unknown_notary_error_reports_profile(self):\n159|        stub = ('#!/bin/sh\\necho \"Error: HTTP 500 from the Apple notary service\" >&2\\n'\n160|                'echo \"Try again later.\" >&2\\nexit 1\\n')\n161|        r = self.run_preflight(OTHER_LINES + '\\n' + TEAM_LINE, stub)\n162|        self.assertNotEqual(r.returncode, 0)\n163|        self.assertIn('notarytool history failed', r.stderr)\n164|        self.assertIn('RunnerControl-notary', r.stderr)\n165|        self.assertIn('HTTP 500', r.stderr)\n166|        self.assertNotIn('locked', r.stderr)\n167|        self.assertNotIn('missing from the login keychain', r.stderr)\n168|\n169|\n170|if __name__ == '__main__':\n171|    unittest.main()","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c677","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a834-2dd6-7302-a20b-bd6ef471e4be"},"sequence":406,"recorded_at":1780531400000807,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f40cada4-f145-4b44-bc35-1e9f8e45782b","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f40cada4-f145-4b44-bc35-1e9f8e45782b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f40cada4-f145-4b44-bc35-1e9f8e45782b"},"call_id":"call_01a0a83559c777edb574545d251f165f","text":"Read text file `Scripts/tests/test_release_metadata.py`.\n1|import base64\n2|import copy\n3|import importlib.util\n4|from pathlib import Path\n5|import tempfile\n6|import unittest\n7|\n8|spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('metadata', Path(__file__).parents[1] / 'release_metadata.py')\n9|m = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n10|spec.loader.exec_module(m)\n11|\n12|class ReleaseMetadataTests(unittest.TestCase):\n13|    def setUp(self):\n14|        self.config = {'marketing_version': '1.1.0', 'bundle_id': 'works.relux.runnercontrol',\n15|                       'team_id': '262RZ595FP', 'macos': {'info_plist': {\n16|                           'SUFeedURL': m.FEED, 'SUPublicEDKey': base64.b64encode(bytes(32)).decode()}}}\n17|    def test_builds_increase_between_attempts_and_runs(self):\n18|        values = [m.prepare(copy.deepcopy(self.config), 'v1.1.0', r, a)['project_version']\n19|                  for r, a in [(1, 1), (1, 2), (2, 1)]]\n20|        self.assertEqual(values, ['101.1', '101.2', '102.1'])\n21|    def test_rejects_wrong_tag_or_identity(self):\n22|        for tag in ['v1.0.0', 'main', 'v1.1.0;echo', 'v1.2', 'v1.2.3.4', '1.1.0', 'v1.1.0 ']:\n23|            with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.prepare(copy.deepcopy(self.config), tag, 1, 1)\n24|        self.config['team_id'] = 'OTHERTEAM'\n25|        with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.prepare(self.config, 'v1.1.0', 1, 1)\n26|    def test_rejects_short_tag_even_when_marketing_matches(self):\n27|        config = copy.deepcopy(self.config)\n28|        config['marketing_version'] = '1.2'\n29|        with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.prepare(config, 'v1.2', 1, 1)\n30|    def test_rejects_invalid_run_attempt_bounds(self):\n31|        for run, attempt in [(0, 1), (9900, 1), (10**6, 1), (1, 0), (1, 100), (1, 10**3)]:\n32|            with self.assertRaises(ValueError):\n33|                m.prepare(copy.deepcopy(self.config), 'v1.1.0', run, attempt)\n34|    def test_accepts_run_attempt_at_exact_limits(self):\n35|        lo = m.prepare(copy.deepcopy(self.config), 'v1.1.0', 1, 1)['project_version']\n36|        hi = m.prepare(copy.deepcopy(self.config), 'v1.1.0', 9899, 99)['project_version']\n37|        self.assertEqual((lo, hi), ('101.1', '9999.99'))\n38|    def test_rejects_bad_sparkle_pubkey(self):\n39|        for raw in (bytes(31), bytes(33), bytes(64)):\n40|            bad = copy.deepcopy(self.config)\n41|            bad['macos']['info_plist']['SUPublicEDKey'] = base64.b64encode(raw).decode()\n42|            with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.prepare(bad, 'v1.1.0', 1, 1)\n43|        bad = copy.deepcopy(self.config)\n44|        bad['macos']['info_plist']['SUPublicEDKey'] = '!!!not-base64!!!'\n45|        with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.prepare(bad, 'v1.1.0', 1, 1)\n46|    def test_rejects_bundle_id_mismatch(self):\n47|        bad = copy.deepcopy(self.config)\n48|        bad['bundle_id'] = 'works.relux.runnercontrol.evil'\n49|        with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.prepare(bad, 'v1.1.0', 1, 1)\n50|    def test_rejects_wrong_feed(self):\n51|        self.config['macos']['info_plist']['SUFeedURL'] = 'https://example.org/feed'\n52|        with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.prepare(self.config, 'v1.1.0', 1, 1)\n53|    def test_appcast_archive_binding(self):\n54|        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n55|            dmg = Path(d) / 'RunnerControl.dmg'; dmg.write_bytes(b'archive')\n56|            feed = Path(d) / 'appcast.xml'\n57|            xml = f'''<rss xmlns:sparkle=\"{m.NS[1:-1]}\"><channel><item>\n58|              <sparkle:version>101.1</sparkle:version><sparkle:shortVersionString>1.1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>\n59|              <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>\n60|              <enclosure url=\"https://github.com/{m.REPO}/releases/download/v1.1.0/RunnerControl.dmg\"\n61|              length=\"7\" sparkle:edSignature=\"{base64.b64encode(bytes(64)).decode()}\"/>\n62|              </item></channel></rss>'''\n63|            feed.write_text(xml)\n64|            m.verify_appcast(feed, dmg, 'v1.1.0', '101.1')\n65|            for bad in [xml.replace('length=\"7\"', 'length=\"8\"'), xml.replace('/v1.1.0/', '/v9.0.0/'),\n66|                        xml.replace('101.1', '100.1'), xml.replace('14.0', '13.0')]:\n67|                feed.write_text(bad)\n68|                with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.verify_appcast(feed, dmg, 'v1.1.0', '101.1')\n69|    def test_rejects_short_version_mismatch(self):\n70|        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n71|            dmg = Path(d) / 'RunnerControl.dmg'; dmg.write_bytes(b'archive')\n72|            feed = Path(d) / 'appcast.xml'\n73|            feed.write_text(_appcast(dmg, short='9.9.9'))\n74|            with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.verify_appcast(feed, dmg, 'v1.1.0', '101.1')\n75|    def test_rejects_wrong_item_count(self):\n76|        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n77|            dmg = Path(d) / 'RunnerControl.dmg'; dmg.write_bytes(b'archive')\n78|            feed = Path(d) / 'appcast.xml'\n79|            feed.write_text(_appcast(dmg, items=0))\n80|            with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.verify_appcast(feed, dmg, 'v1.1.0', '101.1')\n81|            feed.write_text(_appcast(dmg, items=2))\n82|            with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.verify_appcast(feed, dmg, 'v1.1.0', '101.1')\n83|    def test_rejects_bad_signature(self):\n84|        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n85|            dmg = Path(d) / 'RunnerControl.dmg'; dmg.write_bytes(b'archive')\n86|            feed = Path(d) / 'appcast.xml'\n87|            for sig in ['', base64.b64encode(bytes(32)).decode(), '!!!not-base64!!!']:\n88|                feed.write_text(_appcast(dmg, sig=sig))\n89|                with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.verify_appcast(feed, dmg, 'v1.1.0', '101.1')\n90|    def test_rejects_missing_enclosure_and_minimum(self):\n91|        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n92|            dmg = Path(d) / 'RunnerControl.dmg'; dmg.write_bytes(b'archive')\n93|            feed = Path(d) / 'appcast.xml'\n94|            feed.write_text(_appcast(dmg, enclosure=False))\n95|            with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.verify_appcast(feed, dmg, 'v1.1.0', '101.1')\n96|            feed.write_text(_appcast(dmg, minimum=None))\n97|            with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.verify_appcast(feed, dmg, 'v1.1.0', '101.1')\n98|    def test_malformed_appcast_fails_closed(self):\n99|        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n100|            dmg = Path(d) / 'RunnerControl.dmg'; dmg.write_bytes(b'archive')\n101|            feed = Path(d) / 'appcast.xml'; feed.write_text('<rss><channel><item>')\n102|            import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\n103|            with self.assertRaises(ET.ParseError): m.verify_appcast(feed, dmg, 'v1.1.0', '101.1')\n104|\n105|\n106|def _appcast(dmg, short='1.1.0', build='101.1', sig=None, items=1, enclosure=True, minimum='14.0'):\n107|    sig = base64.b64encode(bytes(64)).decode() if sig is None else sig\n108|    enc = (f'<enclosure url=\"https://github.com/{m.REPO}/releases/download/v1.1.0/RunnerControl.dmg\" '\n109|           f'length=\"{dmg.stat().st_size}\" sparkle:edSignature=\"{sig}\"/>') if enclosure else ''\n110|    mintag = f'<sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>{minimum}</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>' if minimum else ''\n111|    item = (f'<item><sparkle:version>{build}</sparkle:version>'\n112|            f'<sparkle:shortVersionString>{short}</sparkle:shortVersionString>{mintag}{enc}</item>')\n113|    return (f'<rss xmlns:sparkle=\"{m.NS[1:-1]}\"><channel>' + item * items + '</channel></rss>')\n114|\n115|TEAM = '262RZ595FP'\n116|EXPECTED_SHA = '267D90FC976A48CF830BE7F41AE612999E025054'\n117|FIND_IDENTITY = (\n118|    '  1) 7FB8D981868F2637B75DFD098A1F87E0CC11158D \"Apple Development: Ivan Oparin (45W9YW7M6V)\"\\n'\n119|    '  2) 08EF92AE3835F98861F51E625FAA9B6900A075C7 \"Apple Development: Ivan Oparin (FSPBF3QRXT)\"\\n'\n120|    f'  3) {EXPECTED_SHA} \"Developer ID Application: Relux Works, LLC ({TEAM})\"\\n'\n121|    '  4) C8448515B5871071F90EB0168A79DCD35E7CA9FE \"Developer ID Application: SKL VC DMCC (4Y4UJAT8QR)\"\\n'\n122|    '     4 valid identities found\\n')\n123|\n124|class SigningIdentityTests(unittest.TestCase):\n125|    def test_returns_team_identity_ignoring_other_teams(self):\n126|        self.assertEqual(m.resolve_signing_identity(FIND_IDENTITY, TEAM), EXPECTED_SHA)\n127|    def test_rejects_missing_team_identity(self):\n128|        only_other = '\\n'.join(l for l in FIND_IDENTITY.splitlines() if TEAM not in l)\n129|        with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.resolve_signing_identity(only_other, TEAM)\n130|    def test_rejects_apple_development_only(self):\n131|        dev_only = '\\n'.join(l for l in FIND_IDENTITY.splitlines() if 'Apple Development' in l)\n132|        with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.resolve_signing_identity(dev_only, TEAM)\n133|    def test_rejects_same_team_apple_development(self):\n134|        same_team_dev = FIND_IDENTITY.splitlines()[0].replace('(45W9YW7M6V)', f'({TEAM})')\n135|        with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.resolve_signing_identity(same_team_dev, TEAM)\n136|    def test_rejects_near_match_team(self):\n137|        near = FIND_IDENTITY.replace(f'({TEAM})', '(262RZ595FX)')\n138|        with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.resolve_signing_identity(near, TEAM)\n139|    def test_rejects_multiple_team_identities(self):\n140|        extra = FIND_IDENTITY.replace('  4) C8448515B5871071F90EB0168A79DCD35E7CA9FE \"Developer ID Application: SKL VC DMCC (4Y4UJAT8QR)\"',\n141|                                      f'  4) AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA \"Developer ID Application: Relux Works, LLC ({TEAM})\"')\n142|        with self.assertRaises(ValueError): m.resolve_signing_identity(extra, TEAM)\n143|\n144|class ReleaseWiringTests(unittest.TestCase):\n145|    def test_release_signs_dmg_with_resolved_team_identity(self):\n146|        lines = (Path(__file__).parents[1] / 'release.sh').read_text().splitlines()\n147|        live = [l for l in lines if not l.lstrip().startswith('#')]\n148|        self.assertTrue(any('release_metadata.py signing-identity' in l and '--team 262RZ595FP' in l for l in live),\n149|                        'release.sh must resolve the DMG signing identity through release_metadata.py signing-identity')","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
