{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7e1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a834-2dd6-7302-a20b-bd6ef471e4be"},"sequence":587,"recorded_at":1780531400001169,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f40cada4-f145-4b44-bc35-1e9f8e45782b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f40cada4-f145-4b44-bc35-1e9f8e45782b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f40cada4-f145-4b44-bc35-1e9f8e45782b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a836-619c-78e0-bb15-7dccf823daf9"},"task_id":"01a0a836-619c-78e0-bb15-7dccf823daf9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a836-619c-78e0-bb15-7dccf823daf9","chunk":"{\"query\":\"gh release view not found error message \\\"not found\\\" missing release\",\"results\":[{\"url\":\"https://github.com/leonarduk/cicaid/issues/71\",\"title\":\"Distinguish between \\\"release not found\\\" and other `gh release view` failures for better error messages\",\"snippet\":\"Release doesn't exist — proceed with create path ... echo \\\"Error checking for release: $output\\\" >&2\\n       exit 1 ... Alternatively, use `gh release view \\\"$TAG\\\" --json tagName` and check for a specific error message pattern, or use `gh api` directly to check the release endpoint and inspect the HTTP status code. ... Ensure the error message includes the original stderr output so users can diagnose the underlying issue.\",\"page_last_modified\":1786142464},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/valory-xyz/olas-operate-app/commit/08a0a4435b4da8a429c97a7e9cfc7fc23aeff22b\",\"title\":\"valory-xyz/olas-operate-app - ci(release): distinguish release-missing from transient gh failures\",\"snippet\":\"valory-xyz/olas-operate-app - ci(release): distinguish release-missing from transient gh failures\\n\\nThe draft-verification step treated any ... \\\"missing\\\" when gh's stderr actually says \\\"release not found\\\"; any other\\nfailure now surfaces with its real error text. Mirrors the existing pattern\\nin check-release-not-published.yml.\\n\\nAddresses review feedback on PR #1977.\\n\\nFiles (1): .github/workflows/publish-release.yml\\nLanguages: TypeScript\\nRepository: valory-xyz/olas-operate-app (17 stars) | Date: 20\",\"page_last_modified\":1779277568},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/xephylon/immaterial-impulse/commit/cb37788153f6722538c5cb41dac544fd5b52d71b\",\"title\":\"xephylon/immaterial-impulse - tools(repo-status): tell a missing release apart from an unreachable one\",\"snippet\":\"xephylon/immaterial-impulse ... practice. It piped `gh release view` into a parser whose `except` printed\\n-1, and -1 was read as \\\"no published release for $pin — installs silently\\nfall back to a source build\\\". But `gh` failing is also an empty stdin, so ... ⚠ rather than being counted as an absent release.\\n\\nVerified by pointing the script at a `gh` stub that fails the way an\\noffline run does - before: \\\"✗ no published release for v0.2.2\\\", after:\\n\\\"⚠ could not query the release for v0.2.2 (error co\",\"page_last_modified\":1785845632},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/14063\",\"title\":\"`gh release create` always blames the missing `workflow` scope on any 404\",\"snippet\":\"Failed to create release, \\\"workflow\\\" scope may be required.\\nTo request it, run: ... gh auth refresh -h github.com -s workflow ... Three things to note in that transcript:\\n\\n- `X-Oauth-Scopes` on the failing response ends in `workflow`, so the token has the scope and the header carrying that fact reached `gh` intact. ... Note the `, ` separator.\\n- The body says `\\\"message\\\": \\\"Not Found\\\"` — the repository does not exist. That is the error the user needed to see\",\"page_last_modified\":1785849984},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/breezyslasher/vita_plex/commit/0a25329411553161a61f1a8d9cd466e8d604d22c\",\"title\":\"breezyslasher/vita_plex - fix(ci): detect a missing release by exit status, not by empty output\",\"snippet\":\"breezyslasher/vita_plex - fix(ci): detect a missing release by exit status, not by empty output\\n\\nThe clear step failed on the case it exists to handle -- no release for ... unsupported protocol scheme \\\"\\\"\\n\\ngh api prints the error body to stdout on a 404 and exits non-zero, so\\ncapturing its output gave a non-empty id of {\\\"message\\\":\\\"Not Found\\\",...}, ... a release id.\\n\\nNow ... gh's real 404 behaviour: missing tag exits 0 without deleting, an existing\\npre-release is deleted, and a non-pre-release is \",\"page_last_modified\":1787066496},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/vm0-ai/vm0/issues/10240\",\"title\":\"bug(ci): rollback-runner workflow false-fails because gh cli not in toolchain-rust image\",\"snippet\":\"gh release view \\\"$TAG\\\" --json assets --jq '.assets[].name' 2>/dev/null | grep -qx \\\"$ASSET_NAME\\\"; then ... echo \\\"::error::Release $TAG does not exist or is missing asset $ASSET_NAME.\\\" ... GH_TOKEN: ***\\n      VERSION: 0.86.4\",\"page_last_modified\":1776672640},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/vm0-ai/vm0/pull/10245\",\"title\":\"vm0-ai/vm0 - fix(ci): replace gh with curl in rollback preflight\",\"snippet\":\"vm0-ai/vm0 fix(ci): replace gh with curl in rollback preflight ... - The `Verify target release asset exists` step in `rollback-runner.yml` calls `gh release view`, but the job's container (`vm0-toolchain-rust`) doesn't ship `gh` — only the local `development` stage does. ... With `2>/dev/null` swallowing the `gh: not found` error and POSIX `sh -e` having no pipefail, every production rollback false-fails at the preflight with a misleading \\\"release does not exist\\\" message.\",\"page_last_modified\":1776744320},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/githubnext/gh-aw/issues/10504\",\"title\":\"[CI Failure Doctor] CI Failure Investigation - SBOM Upload Timing Change (Run #21102091204)\",\"snippet\":\"**Examine SBOM upload step specifically**:\\n   ```bash\\n   gh run view 21102091204 --log | grep -A 20 \\\"Upload SBOM files to release\\\" ... GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\\n    RELEASE_TAG: ${{ needs.config.outputs.release_tag }}\\n  run: |\\n    set -e  # Exit on any error ... *.json || echo \\\"ERROR: SBOM files not found\\\" ... gh release view \\\"$RELEASE_TAG\\\" > /dev/null 2>&1; then\",\"page_last_modified\":1768691200},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/aikdna/kdna-studio-cli/issues/12\",\"title\":\"[Release] 0.6.1 published to npm but no GitHub tag, no GitHub release, no CHANGELOG entry\",\"snippet\":\"The first occurrence triggered issue #22 (ajv error message) to be raised as a sibling; closing it without addressing the silent-patch pipeline allows the pattern to continue. ... - `gh release view v0.6.1 --repo aikdna/kdna-studio-cli` → \\\"release not found\\\"\\n- CHANGELOG.md: still ends at v0.5.9 (or wherever the last documented release is)\",\"page_last_modified\":1782089472},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/te-toshiakitanaka2/kale/blob/HEAD/.claude/skills/release/SKILL.md\",\"title\":\"te-toshiakitanaka2/kale - .claude/skills/release/SKILL.md\",\"snippet\":\"**Duplicate-release guard** — `gh release view v{new}` must fail with not-found. Abort if a Release already exists.\",\"page_last_modified\":1779056256}]}","final_result":true}}}
